<title>USA: Individual Investor Q3 shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Individual Investor Q3 shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>INDIVIDUAL INVESTOR GROUP, INC. AND</p>
<p>SUBSIDIARIES			   Three Months	   Nine</p>
<p>Months</p>
<p>			   1996	1995	  1996	 1995</p>
<p>Total Revenues     2,537,398  2,131,744  8,745,213  6,140,519</p>
<p>Total Operating</p>
<p> Expenses	    4,129,004  2,632,190 10,934,556  7,019,322</p>
<p>Operating loss    (1,591,606)  (500,446)(2,189,343)  (878,803)</p>
<p>Interest and other</p>
<p> income		   27,333  1,005,113    155,744   1,031,328</p>
<p>Net (loss) income($1,564,273)  $504,667 (2,033,599)    152,525</p>
<p>EPS			 ($0.26)     $0.09     ($0.33)	$0.03</p>
<p>Avg shares	   6,091,412  7,136,796  6,222,870   4,678,706</p>
<p>NOTE: Beginning in the third quarter 1996, the company reclassified its statement of operations and is now recording equity in (loss) income of affiliates under operating revenues so they are reflected as part of core operations. Third quarter 1995 included other income of about $1 million from the sale of a marketable security. Net loss in 3Q 1996 includes equity in net loss of affiliate of $773,847 vs equity in net income of affiliate of $78,616 in 3Q 1995.</p>
